ownload_count":52,"created_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:05Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:07Z"},{"id":703621042,"node_id":"RA_kwDOGxaghM4p8Gey","name":"mirrord_mac_universal","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":407473216,"digest":"sha256:fb275886ec139ff38a7d0beaa68fb9999c2cfb40cca26264d41d33834a3a2b81","download_count":467,"created_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:05Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:25Z"},{"id":703621025,"node_id":"RA_kwDOGxaghM4p8Geh","name":"mirrord_mac_universal.shasum256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":92,"digest":"sha256:639e1fcb47ffae3b0ce6c3f4d221f194782d41c23f27a6ca6d694f7e610d1fc3","download_count":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:05Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:06Z"},{"id":703621037,"node_id":"RA_kwDOGxaghM4p8Get","name":"mirrord_mac_universal.zip","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":161456715,"digest":"sha256:947ab066839e540ec52b78ee2e847f1317f9dcd8a5562c925616c2d725a353f0","download_count":106,"created_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:05Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T00:02:13Z"}],"body":"\n\n### Added\n\n- Added `db_branching` to `mirrord-up.yaml` modes: `empty`, `schema` or `all`\n  requests every `MirrordSplitConfig` DB branch with that copy mode, `inherit`\n  with each entry's own, `off` none. An entry named `split`, `replace` or\n  `mirror` may set it for that built-in mode. A mode without it branches like\n  the built-in mode its `incoming` names, and a mode without `queues` splits\n  them like its `incoming`: mirrored with `incoming: mirror`, stolen otherwise.\n  In `mirrord.json`, `feature.db_branches` takes `{ \"entries\": \"*\", \"copy\": {\n  \"mode\": \"schema\" } }` to request a copy mode. `mirrord up` fails before\n  starting any service when a mode's `db_branching` or `queues` line can't be\n  served: no usable operator (saying why), no DB branch definitions, an entry's\n  database engine turned off in the operator, a copy mode outside an entry's\n  `allowedModes`, or an operator that splits no queues. It also fails up front\n  when services sharing a DB branch ask for different copy modes.\n- Added custom modes to `mirrord-up.yaml`: a `modes` entry sets `incoming` and\n  `queues`, and is selected by name with `default_mode` or `mirrord up --mode`.\n\n\n### Changed\n\n- On Linux, `experimental.hook_libc_syscall` and\n  `experimental.old_glibc_support` are now enabled by default for OSS users.\n\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed the layer losing its internal proxy connection when an application\n  reuses low fd numbers, such as the s6-overlay `/init` script.\n\n"}
